  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001154",
        "SRC-001155"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Almanac (2023): Willow Commons at 4388 Alpine Road, next to Roberts Market in the Nathhorst Triangle, has 11 one-bedroom apartments under 500 sq ft for adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities, 2 staff units, an attached ADU and a detached two-bedroom ADU of about 870 sq ft. Buildings are set back about 75 feet from the street. The Whites acquired adjacent 4394 Alpine Road in 2021.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004004"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Almanac (2025): the complex houses 16 tenants, with 40% of its square footage as community space. Common Grounds, a coffee shop staffed by residents and operated with Cat and Cloud, is planned to open by 2026. Jim White said permit delays cost the project about $1 million and a year.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004003"
      ]
    }
  ],
